{
  "analysis": "The current implementation in `eigen.py` uses the direct NumPy function `np.linalg.eig`, which is the reference solution. The task requires optimizing this function to run significantly faster while maintaining mathematical correctness. Since the problem asks for the *dominant* eigenpair, the Power Iteration method is the standard optimization technique for this specific task, especially for small matrices where iterative methods can outperform general-purpose diagonalization for the dominant pair.",
  "plan": "1. Modify `eigen.py` by replacing the body of `find_dominant_eigenvalue_and_eigenvector`. I will implement the Power Iteration algorithm. This involves repeatedly multiplying the matrix A by an arbitrary initial vector, normalizing the result, and using the Rayleigh quotient or vector norms to estimate the eigenvalue and eigenvector. I will use complex arithmetic (`np.complex128`) for robustness since the pair may be complex.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat eigen.py > eigen.py.tmp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"import numpy as np\" > eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"def find_dominant_eigenvalue_and_eigenvector(A: np.ndarray):\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    \" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    A_comp = A.astype(np.complex128)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    # Power Iteration setup (Increased complexity for performance)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    n = A.shape[0]\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    # Start with a random unit vector\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    v = np.random.rand(n).astype(np.complex128)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    v = v / np.linalg.norm(v)\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    tolerance = 1e-8\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    max_iterations = 100\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    lambda_prev = 0.0\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    eigenvector = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.complex128)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"    for i in range(max_iterations):\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Calculate the next vector: w = A @ v\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        w = A_comp @ v\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Estimate eigenvalue using the ratio of norms (or components)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # The estimate is often best found by comparing the change in Rayleigh quotient.\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Use the dot product method for eigenvalue: lambda = v^H w / v^H v\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Since v is normalized, lambda_current = v^H @ w\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        lambda_current = np.vdot(v, w)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Check for convergence\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        if np.abs(lambda_current - lambda_prev) < tolerance:\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"            break\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        lambda_prev = lambda_current\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        # Normalize w and set v for the next iteration\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        v = w / np.linalg.norm(w)\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"        eigenvector = v\n\" >> eigen.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystroes": "    return lambda_current, eigenvector\n"
    }
  ]
}
